1
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
He's up past his bedtime in the city that never sleeps.

2
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Home Alone 2: Lost in New York is a comedy, family,
adventure film directed by Chris Columbus.

3
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Instead of flying to Florida with his folks, Kevin ends up alone in New York, where he gets a hotel
room with his dad's credit card—despite problems from a clerk and meddling bellboy.

4
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
But when Kevin runs into his old nemeses, the Wet Bandits, he's determined
to foil their plans to rob a toy store on Christmas Eve.

5
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Kevin, played by Macaulay Culkin.

6
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Harry, played by Joe Pesci.

7
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Marv, played by Daniel Stern.

8
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Kate, played by Catherine O'Hara.

9
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Peter, played by John Heard.

10
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Pigeon Lady, played by Brenda Fricker.

11
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Home Alone 2: Lost in New York is a 1992 American Christmas comedy film
directed by Chris Columbus and written and produced by John Hughes.

12
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
The sequel to Home Alone (1990) and the second installment in the Home Alone franchise, the film stars Macaulay
Culkin, Joe Pesci, Daniel Stern, John Heard, Tim Curry, Brenda Fricker and Catherine O'Hara.

13
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
The story follows Kevin McCallister as he is separated from his family on
their vacation to Miami, Florida and ends up in New York City.

14
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
While initially enjoying his newfound experiences, Kevin soon encounters
the Wet Bandits again after their escape from prison.

15
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Hughes finished writing the film by February 1991, after
signing a six-picture deal with 20th Century Fox.

16
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
Culkin's return was confirmed in May and the rest of
the cast was finalized soon after.

17
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Principal photography took place between December 1991 and May 1992 on location in Illinois and
New York, including at the Rockefeller Center and the original World Trade Center.

18
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Home Alone 2 was theatrically released in the United States
by 20th Century Fox on November 20, 1992.

19
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
It received mixed reviews from critics.

20
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
However, Home Alone 2 grossed over $359 million worldwide; it
became the third-highest-grossing film of 1992.

21
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Home Alone 2 is the only Home Alone sequel to feature the
majority of the cast from the first film.

22
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
Home Alone 3 (1997) featured a new cast and characters, and the television film Home Alone 4
(2002) recast returning characters from the first two films to new actors.

23
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
The film explores themes of new york city, burglar,
holiday, family relationships, sequel.

24
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:18,000
The tone is lighthearted.
